# Fetch the connected board's identity on demand.
#
# The same information is published on the board_info topic with transient_local
# durability, so most clients never need this. It exists for the case that
# topic cannot serve: a caller that wants to know whether the board is
# answering *right now*, rather than what it last said.
---
# False when no board has identified itself yet, in which case info is unset
# and message says why. A driver that has never heard from the board must say
# so rather than return a zeroed struct that reads like firmware 0.0.
bool available
string message
BoardInfo info
